From 63046ca3fb71c876e94f9bab337cf25e8785edbb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "kevin.krausse" <kkrausse97@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 02:06:21 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 2/8] web: pk-web browser module; 1 MiB stream buffer in the
 tensor loader

examples/web builds an ES6 Emscripten module (JSPI or ASYNCIFY per
GGML_WEBGPU_JSPI) exposing pk_load / pk_run / pk_json for a page or worker.
The model is read from the Emscripten FS, which a worker backs with OPFS or a
Blob so the file is never copied whole into the WASM heap.

Loader: give the tensor-data ifstream a 1 MiB buffer. libc++ refills 4 KiB at
a time; through WORKERFS every refill is a synchronous Blob slice and the
Q8_0 model took 171 s to load in Chrome. With the buffer: 4.9 s through a
Blob, 1.3 s through an OPFS sync access handle.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
